<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="50–60 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 9</p>
  <h1>First conditional <em>an open condition and its result</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Build a useful response before the future is settled: <span class="ex">If the rain starts, we’ll move check-in inside. If the side door is open, volunteers can use it. If the boxes arrive early, put them in storage.</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">50–60 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">if · when · unless</span>
    <span class="tag">condition · result · speaker framing</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Separate an unsettled condition from the response it activates.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Find future reference in a present-form condition clause.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Control clause order, result types, when, and unless.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Give a fictional contingency briefing and answer follow-ups.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can state an open future condition, choose a prediction, plan, possibility, permission, or instruction as its result, order and punctuate both clauses, distinguish <span class="ex">if</span> from expected-time <span class="ex">when</span>, and use <span class="ex">unless</span> for an exception.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved a future prediction, present-simple agreement, and a direct instruction.">
    <h3>Three checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Use the stated time, subject, and sentence purpose.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Earlier lesson choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will">will</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="does">does</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="starts">starts</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="start">start</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Move">Move</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Moves">Moves</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The coordinator makes a neutral prediction about tomorrow: The weather report says it <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will" data-hint="Will plus a base verb presents the prediction about tomorrow." data-fix="The weather report says it will rain tomorrow." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> rain tomorrow.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The singular subject inspection takes third-person present agreement: The inspection <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="starts" data-hint="A present-simple statement with singular inspection adds s." data-fix="The inspection starts at eight." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at eight.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Give a direct instruction about the boxes: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Move" data-hint="A positive imperative begins with the base verb." data-fix="Move the boxes into storage." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the boxes into storage.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice one event plan with different results</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Riverside workshop contingency board</h3>
    <p><b>Open weather condition:</b> <span class="ex">If the rain starts before nine, we’ll move check-in inside.</span></p>
    <p><b>Permission:</b> <span class="ex">If the side door is open, volunteers can use it.</span></p>
    <p><b>Instruction:</b> <span class="ex">If the boxes arrive early, put them in storage.</span></p>
    <p><b>Expected scheduled event:</b> <span class="ex">When the coordinator arrives at eight, she’ll open the office.</span></p>
    <p><b>Exception:</b> <span class="ex">Unless the inspection runs late, the doors will open at nine.</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which clauses name a condition or time situation? Which clauses give its result?</li>
      <li>Does every result use <span class="ex">will</span>?</li>
      <li>Which marker leaves the event open, which presents it as expected, and which means “except if”?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You separated an open condition, predicted plan, permission, instruction, expected time event, and exception.">
    <h3>Discovery check: identify the clause’s job</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Condition and result choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="open condition">open condition</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="predicted plan">predicted plan</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="permission">permission</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="instruction">instruction</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="expected time event">expected time event</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="exception">exception</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The team does not know whether rain will begin before nine: <span class="ex">If the rain starts before nine</span> names an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="open condition" data-hint="If leaves the weather condition unsettled in this plan." data-fix="If the rain starts before nine names an open condition." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The team’s planned response to that weather is <span class="ex">we’ll move check-in inside</span>, a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="predicted plan" data-hint="Will presents what the team plans or predicts as the response." data-fix="We’ll move check-in inside gives the predicted plan." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><span class="ex">Volunteers can use it</span> tells what becomes allowed if the door is open, so the result gives <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="permission" data-hint="Can marks permission in this result clause." data-fix="Volunteers can use it gives permission." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><span class="ex">Put them in storage</span> tells the listener what to do after an early arrival, so the result gives an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="instruction" data-hint="The base verb put begins an imperative result." data-fix="Put them in storage gives an instruction." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The schedule treats the coordinator’s eight o’clock arrival as part of the expected timeline: the <span class="ex">when</span> clause names an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="expected time event" data-hint="When presents the arrival as expected in the plan." data-fix="When the coordinator arrives at eight names an expected time event." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span><span class="ex">Unless the inspection runs late</span> means the doors open except in one case, so it names an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="exception" data-hint="Unless introduces the case that can prevent the result." data-fix="Unless the inspection runs late introduces an exception." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: one situation activates another</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A first conditional presents a future condition as open and relevant. The speaker does not commit to whether it will happen. The result says what becomes true, possible, permitted, planned, or necessary if that condition is met.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>clause</th><th>job</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>condition</td><td>states the situation that activates the result</td><td><span class="ex">if the rain starts</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>result</td><td>states the consequence or response</td><td><span class="ex">we’ll move check-in inside</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">An open condition is not automatically unlikely, and the first conditional does not promise that its result is objectively “likely.” It shows the speaker’s chosen connection between a possible condition and its consequence. Evidence and context determine probability.</p>

  <h2>Build the core future pattern without a false absolute</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>In the core pattern, use a present form in the future condition clause and <span class="ex">will / won’t + base verb</span> for a predicted or planned result.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>order</th><th>form and punctuation</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>condition first</td><td><span class="ex">If + present, will + base</span>; add a comma after the first clause</td><td><span class="ex">If it rains, we’ll move inside.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>result first</td><td><span class="ex">Will + base + if + present</span>; normally no comma in this short pattern</td><td><span class="ex">We’ll move inside if it rains.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>question about the result</td><td>question order in the result; present order after <span class="ex">if</span></td><td><span class="ex">What will we do if it rains?</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>The two orders keep the same basic condition-result relationship, but they can change information flow and emphasis. Condition-first order sets the situation before the response. Result-first order can foreground the response.</p>
  <p class="note-line">Do not put <span class="ex">will</span> in the condition clause merely to mark future time: say <span class="ex">If it rains, we’ll move inside</span>, not <span class="ex">If it will rain, we’ll move inside</span>. English can use <span class="ex">will</span> after <span class="ex">if</span> for special meanings such as willingness, but that is not the future marker taught in this A2 pattern.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You controlled future-reference present form, third-person agreement, result will, negative condition, question order, and clause order.">
    <h3>Drill 1: complete the core form</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="First-conditional form choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="starts">starts</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will start">will start</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="runs">runs</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="run">run</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="we’ll move">we’ll move</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="we move">we move</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="doesn’t arrive">doesn’t arrive</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="won’t arrive">won’t arrive</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will">will</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="do">do</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="arrives">arrives</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will arrive">will arrive</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The rain condition has future reference but uses present agreement: If the rain <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="starts" data-hint="In the core future condition, singular rain takes present starts." data-fix="If the rain starts, we’ll move check-in inside." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>, we’ll move check-in inside.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The singular inspection keeps third-person present agreement after <span class="ex">if</span>: If the inspection <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="runs" data-hint="Inspection is singular, so the present form is runs." data-fix="If the inspection runs late, the doors will open at ten." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> late, the doors will open at ten.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The team’s planned response uses <span class="ex">will + base verb</span>: If the rain starts, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="we’ll move" data-hint="The planned result uses we’ll plus base move." data-fix="If the rain starts, we’ll move check-in inside." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> check-in inside.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The negative condition refers to a key that may fail to arrive: If the key <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="doesn’t arrive" data-hint="Use present doesn’t arrive in the future condition clause." data-fix="If the key doesn’t arrive, call the coordinator." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>, call the coordinator.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Ask about the future result, then keep present order in the <span class="ex">if</span> clause: What <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will" data-hint="The result question uses will before the subject we." data-fix="What will we do if the rain starts?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> we do if the rain starts?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The result comes first, so the short final condition normally has no comma: The office will open at eight if the coordinator <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="arrives" data-hint="The future condition uses present arrives after if." data-fix="The office will open at eight if the coordinator arrives on time." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> on time.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose a result that matches the speaker’s purpose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The result clause is not limited to <span class="ex">will</span>. Choose the form that expresses the response you mean.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>result purpose</th><th>form</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>prediction or plan</td><td><span class="ex">will / won’t</span></td><td><span class="ex">If it rains, we’ll move inside.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>weaker possibility</td><td><span class="ex">may / might</span></td><td><span class="ex">If traffic is heavy, the driver might arrive late.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>permission or available possibility</td><td><span class="ex">can</span></td><td><span class="ex">If the side door is open, volunteers can use it.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>instruction or advice</td><td>imperative</td><td><span class="ex">If the key doesn’t arrive, call the coordinator.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You matched the open condition to a plan, weaker possibility, permission, instruction, warning, and question.">
    <h3>Drill 2: choose the result purpose</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Conditional result choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="we’ll move">we’ll move</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="might arrive">might arrive</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="can use">can use</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="call">call</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="won’t open">won’t open</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will you do">will you do</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The board states the team’s planned response: If the rain begins, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="we’ll move" data-hint="Will presents the team’s contingency plan." data-fix="If the rain begins, we’ll move check-in inside." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> check-in inside.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The delay is possible but not the coordinator’s firm prediction: If traffic is heavy, the driver <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="might arrive" data-hint="Might marks the weaker possible result requested in the context." data-fix="If traffic is heavy, the driver might arrive late." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> late.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The open side door makes this route available to volunteers: If the side door is open, volunteers <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can use" data-hint="Can expresses permission or available possibility." data-fix="If the side door is open, volunteers can use it." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> it.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The result is a direct instruction to the listener: If the key doesn’t arrive, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="call" data-hint="An imperative result begins with the base verb call." data-fix="If the key doesn’t arrive, call the coordinator." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the coordinator.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The notice warns about the consequence of a late inspection: The doors <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="won’t open" data-hint="Won’t presents the negative predicted consequence." data-fix="The doors won’t open at nine if the inspection runs late." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at nine if the inspection runs late.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Ask the listener to choose a response to the open condition: What <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will you do" data-hint="The result question uses will before subject you and base do." data-fix="What will you do if the delivery is late?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> if the delivery is late?</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Frame the future with <em>if</em>, <em>when</em>, or <em>unless</em></h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>marker</th><th>speaker’s framing</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>if</b></td><td>leaves the condition open</td><td><span class="ex">If the rain starts, we’ll move inside.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>when</b></td><td>presents the time event as expected</td><td><span class="ex">When the coordinator arrives, she’ll open the office.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>unless</b></td><td>means “except if” or, in the core pattern, “if not”</td><td><span class="ex">Unless the inspection runs late, we’ll open at nine.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><span class="ex">When</span> shows the speaker’s expectation; it does not guarantee the event in the real world. The same future can be framed differently: <span class="ex">When the delivery arrives, we’ll unload it</span> treats arrival as expected, while <span class="ex">If the delivery arrives by eight, we’ll unload it before opening</span> leaves the deadline condition open.</p>
  <p class="note-line">In this A2 pattern, <span class="ex">unless the inspection runs late</span> equals <span class="ex">if the inspection does not run late</span>. Do not add another negative when making that replacement: not <span class="ex">unless the inspection doesn’t run late</span> for the same meaning. Like <span class="ex">if</span> and future <span class="ex">when</span>, <span class="ex">unless</span> uses a present form rather than <span class="ex">will</span> merely to mark future time.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You chose an open condition, expected time event, exception, accurate negative replacement, present future-time form, and condition-first comma.">
    <h3>Drill 3: choose the marker and framing</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="If when and unless choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="If">If</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="When">When</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Unless">Unless</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="if the inspection does not run late">if the inspection does not run late</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="arrives">arrives</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="comma">comma</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The team does not know whether the rain will begin before nine: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="If" data-hint="If leaves the weather condition open." data-fix="If the rain begins before nine, we’ll move check-in inside." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the rain begins before nine, we’ll move check-in inside.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The published schedule presents the coordinator’s eight o’clock arrival as expected: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="When" data-hint="When presents the scheduled arrival as expected." data-fix="When the coordinator arrives at eight, she’ll open the office." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the coordinator arrives at eight, she’ll open the office.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The doors open at nine except if the inspection runs late: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Unless" data-hint="Unless introduces the exception that prevents the normal result." data-fix="Unless the inspection runs late, the doors will open at nine." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the inspection runs late, the doors will open at nine.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Replace <span class="ex">unless the inspection runs late</span> without changing its core meaning: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="if the inspection does not run late" data-hint="Unless plus a positive clause becomes if plus a negative clause." data-fix="If the inspection does not run late, the doors will open at nine." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>, the doors will open at nine.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The arrival is future, but the expected-time clause uses present agreement: When the driver <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="arrives" data-hint="Future when clauses use a present form in this pattern." data-fix="When the driver arrives, we’ll unload the boxes." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>, we’ll unload the boxes.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The condition clause comes first, so place a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="comma" data-hint="A first condition clause is followed by a comma before its result." data-fix="If the key arrives, we’ll open the office." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> after it before writing the result.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Sound natural: make the condition and response one path</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>With the condition first, use two connected thought groups and a small boundary before the response: <span class="ex">If it <strong>RAINS</strong> | we’ll move <strong>IN</strong>side.</span> With the result first, the sentence often flows through the final condition without a full pause: <span class="ex">We’ll move <strong>IN</strong>side if it <strong>RAINS</strong>.</span></p>
  <p>In connected U.S. speech, <span class="ex">if you</span> often links as /ɪf jə/, and <span class="ex">we’ll</span> is one short syllable, often /wil/ or a lighter /wəl/. Keep the main condition and result words clear. Stress <span class="ex">if</span> only for contrast or correction: <span class="ex"><strong>IF</strong> the rain starts</span> corrects an assumption that rain is certain. <span class="ex">Unless</span> keeps stress on its second syllable: /ənˈlɛs/.</p>

  <section data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read open condition, expected time, exception, predicted plan, weaker possibility, and imperative-result listening check">
    <h2>Listen: how does the speaker frame the path?</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p>Your teacher reads each fictional workshop line once naturally and once more slowly. Listen for the marker, the condition’s status, and the result purpose. Open the script only after checking.</p>
    <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You heard an open condition, expected time event, exception, planned result, weaker possibility, and imperative result.">
      <h3>Tutor-read listening check</h3>
      <div class="quiz-list">
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the rain condition is open" data-hint="If leaves the weather condition unsettled in the speaker’s plan." data-fix="If the rain starts before nine presents the rain condition as open."><p class="quiz-question">1. How does Clip 1 frame the rain?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the rain condition is open">the rain condition is open</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the rain has already started">the rain has already started</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the speaker guarantees rain">the speaker guarantees rain</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the arrival is expected in the schedule" data-hint="When presents the scheduled arrival as expected." data-fix="When the coordinator arrives at eight presents the arrival as expected in the schedule."><p class="quiz-question">2. What does <span class="ex">when</span> communicate in Clip 2?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the arrival is expected in the schedule">the arrival is expected in the schedule</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the coordinator is already in the office">the coordinator is already in the office</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the arrival is impossible">the arrival is impossible</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a late inspection is the exception" data-hint="Unless introduces the one case that prevents opening at nine." data-fix="A late inspection is the exception that can prevent the doors from opening at nine."><p class="quiz-question">3. What can prevent the nine o’clock opening in Clip 3?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a late inspection is the exception">a late inspection is the exception</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="an early delivery is the exception">an early delivery is the exception</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the office always opens at ten">the office always opens at ten</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the team plans to move check-in inside" data-hint="We’ll move presents the team’s planned response." data-fix="If the rain starts, the team plans to move check-in inside."><p class="quiz-question">4. What planned result follows the condition in Clip 4?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the team plans to move check-in inside">the team plans to move check-in inside</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the team will cancel every workshop">the team will cancel every workshop</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="volunteers must leave immediately">volunteers must leave immediately</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a weaker possible delay" data-hint="Might presents lateness as a possible result rather than a firm prediction." data-fix="The driver might arrive late presents a weaker possible delay."><p class="quiz-question">5. What does <span class="ex">might</span> contribute in Clip 5?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a weaker possible delay">a weaker possible delay</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a guaranteed delay">a guaranteed delay</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="permission to cancel the delivery">permission to cancel the delivery</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="call the coordinator" data-hint="The base verb call begins a direct instruction as the result." data-fix="If the key doesn’t arrive, call the coordinator."><p class="quiz-question">6. What instruction does Clip 6 give?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="call the coordinator">call the coordinator</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="wait without telling anyone">wait without telling anyone</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="open the office without a key">open the office without a key</button></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <details class="thinking-card">
      <summary>Open the teacher script after checking</summary>
      <ol>
        <li><span class="ex">If the rain starts before nine, we’ll move check-in inside.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">When the coordinator arrives at eight, she’ll open the office.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">Unless the inspection runs late, the doors will open at nine.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">If the rain starts, we’ll move check-in inside.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">If traffic is heavy, the driver might arrive late.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ex">If the key doesn’t arrive, call the coordinator.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </details>
  </section>

  <h2>Read the 7:45 contingency update</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Message to the Riverside workshop team</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">The inspection is on schedule. Unless it runs late, the doors will open at nine. When the coordinator arrives at eight, she’ll check the office key. If the key doesn’t arrive with her, call the building manager. The forecast is still uncertain. If the rain begins before nine, we’ll move check-in inside. If traffic is heavy, the delivery driver might arrive after opening, but volunteers can start setup if the side door is unlocked.</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You followed the expected event, exception, open weather condition, and weaker delivery possibility.">
    <h3>Reading check: use only the update</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a late inspection" data-hint="Unless identifies the one exception to the nine o’clock opening." data-fix="A late inspection can prevent the doors from opening at nine."><p class="quiz-question">1. What can prevent the doors from opening at nine?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a late inspection">a late inspection</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the coordinator arriving at eight">the coordinator arriving at eight</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the side door being unlocked">the side door being unlocked</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the coordinator’s arrival at eight" data-hint="When frames the scheduled arrival as expected." data-fix="The update presents the coordinator’s arrival at eight as expected."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which event does the writer present as expected?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the coordinator’s arrival at eight">the coordinator’s arrival at eight</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="rain beginning before nine">rain beginning before nine</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the delivery arriving late">the delivery arriving late</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="move check-in inside" data-hint="The sentence after the uncertain forecast gives the weather contingency." data-fix="If rain begins before nine, the team will move check-in inside."><p class="quiz-question">3. What is the team’s plan if rain begins before nine?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="move check-in inside">move check-in inside</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="cancel the inspection">cancel the inspection</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="lock the side door">lock the side door</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the driver’s late arrival is only a possibility" data-hint="Might marks lateness as a weaker possible result." data-fix="If traffic is heavy, the driver’s late arrival is only a possibility."><p class="quiz-question">4. Why does the update use <span class="ex">might arrive</span> for the driver?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the driver’s late arrival is only a possibility">the driver’s late arrival is only a possibility</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the driver is guaranteed to arrive late">the driver is guaranteed to arrive late</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the driver has permission to skip the delivery">the driver has permission to skip the delivery</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build a contingency and an instruction</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="if the inspection ends on time we'll open at nine" data-hint="Begin with If, use present ends in the condition, then we’ll plus base open in the result." data-fix="If the inspection ends on time, we’ll open at nine." data-success-message="Correct. The future condition uses present ends, and the planned result uses we’ll open.">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the condition first</h3><p class="tile-target">The nine o’clock opening depends on the inspection ending on time.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="time">time</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="open">open</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="inspection">inspection</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="if">If</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="nine">nine</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="ends">ends</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="at">at</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="on">on</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="we'll">we’ll</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="call maya if the key doesn't arrive" data-hint="Begin with the imperative call and name Maya, then add the final if clause with present doesn’t arrive." data-fix="Call Maya if the key doesn’t arrive." data-success-message="Correct. The instruction comes first, and the final condition uses present doesn’t arrive without a comma.">
    <h3>Drill 5: build the imperative result first</h3><p class="tile-target">Tell the volunteer what to do if the key fails to arrive.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="key">key</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="if">if</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="arrive">arrive</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="call">Call</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="maya">Maya</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="doesn't">doesn’t</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair three different errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="will" data-hint="The condition refers to the future, but it does not use will merely as a future marker." data-fix="If it rains, we’ll move inside." data-why="Use present rains in the core future condition; keep will in the planned result." data-success-message="Correct. The open future condition uses present rains, not will rain.">
    <h3>Drill 6: future reference without future <em>will</em></h3><p>The plan says: <span class="ex">If it will rain, we’ll move inside.</span> Tap the unnecessary future marker.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="if">If</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="it">it</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="will">will</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="rain">rain</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="we’ll">we’ll</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="move">move inside</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="doesn’t" data-hint="Unless already supplies the negative exception meaning in this intended sentence." data-fix="Unless the inspection runs late, we’ll open at nine." data-why="For the intended meaning, replace if the inspection does not run late with unless the inspection runs late." data-success-message="Correct. Unless already creates the exception, so the controlled replacement uses a positive clause.">
    <h3>Drill 7: avoid the unintended double negative</h3><p>The writer intends “if the inspection does not run late”: <span class="ex">Unless the inspection doesn’t run late, we’ll open at nine.</span> Tap the word that reverses the intended exception.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="unless">Unless</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="inspection">the inspection</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="doesn’t">doesn’t</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="run">run late</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="open">we’ll open</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="nine">at nine</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="arrive" data-hint="The singular subject delivery needs third-person present agreement in the condition." data-fix="If the delivery arrives early, put the boxes in storage." data-why="Future-reference present simple still agrees with its subject: the delivery arrives." data-success-message="Correct. Singular delivery takes present arrives in the condition clause.">
    <h3>Drill 8: keep present agreement</h3><p>The instruction says: <span class="ex">If the delivery arrive early, put the boxes in storage.</span> Tap the verb with missing agreement.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="if">If</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="delivery">the delivery</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="arrive">arrive</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="early">early</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="put">put</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="boxes">the boxes in storage</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Oral transforms: preserve the condition-result relationship</h3>
    <p>Say each complete new sentence before revealing it. Keep the stated framing and purpose.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> <span class="ex">If it rains, we’ll move inside.</span> Put the result first.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>We’ll move inside if it rains.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> The side door may be open. Then volunteers have permission to use it.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>If the side door is open, volunteers can use it.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> The key may not arrive. Give the listener an instruction.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>If the key doesn’t arrive, call the coordinator.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> The inspection normally ends on time. A late inspection is the exception to opening at nine. Use <span class="ex">unless</span>.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Unless the inspection runs late, we’ll open at nine.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> The scheduled coordinator arrival is expected. Use <span class="ex">when</span>.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>When the coordinator arrives, she’ll open the office.</strong></p></div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> Heavy traffic creates only a possible delay. Use <span class="ex">might</span>.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>If traffic is heavy, the driver might arrive late.</strong></p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Communicate: brief a fictional contingency team</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to disclose your real work, school, home, location, schedule, travel, health, finances, family, relationships, safety plans, passwords, weather risks, or future plans. Use the Riverside workshop, invent a neutral public event, or share personal information only when you freely choose.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Ask before briefing:</b> Ask two <span class="ex">What will you do if...?</span> questions about fictional delays or changes. Give one firm plan and one weaker possible result with <span class="ex">might</span>.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Final production: give a 45–60 second fictional contingency briefing.</b> Include two open <span class="ex">if</span> conditions, one expected <span class="ex">when</span> event, one <span class="ex">unless</span> exception, one planned result, one weaker possibility, one permission, and one instruction. Use condition-first and result-first order at least once each.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Reframe one event:</b> Present the same arrival first with <span class="ex">when</span> because the schedule treats it as expected, then with <span class="ex">if...by</span> because meeting a deadline remains open. Explain how the speaker’s framing changes.</div>

  <h2>Final check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You controlled the core future condition, result purpose, unless exception, and expected-versus-open framing.">
    <h3>Four decisions with one defensible target</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="If the rain starts, we’ll move inside." data-hint="The open future condition uses present starts; the planned result uses we’ll move." data-fix="If the rain starts, we’ll move inside."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence uses the core first-conditional form for this open weather contingency?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the rain starts, we’ll move inside.">If the rain starts, we’ll move inside.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the rain will start, we’ll move inside.">If the rain will start, we’ll move inside.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the rain start, we’ll move inside.">If the rain start, we’ll move inside.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="If the key doesn’t arrive, call the coordinator." data-hint="The required response is an instruction, so use an imperative result." data-fix="If the key doesn’t arrive, call the coordinator."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence gives a direct instruction activated by a possible missing key?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the key doesn’t arrive, call the coordinator.">If the key doesn’t arrive, call the coordinator.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the key doesn’t arrive, you might call the coordinator.">If the key doesn’t arrive, you might call the coordinator.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the key won’t arrive, called the coordinator.">If the key won’t arrive, called the coordinator.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Unless the inspection runs late, we’ll open at nine." data-hint="Unless plus a positive clause expresses the exception to the normal opening plan." data-fix="Unless the inspection runs late, we’ll open at nine."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which sentence means “We’ll open at nine if the inspection does not run late”?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Unless the inspection runs late, we’ll open at nine.">Unless the inspection runs late, we’ll open at nine.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Unless the inspection doesn’t run late, we’ll open at nine.">Unless the inspection doesn’t run late, we’ll open at nine.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Unless the inspection will run late, we’ll open at nine.">Unless the inspection will run late, we’ll open at nine.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="When the coordinator arrives, she’ll open the office." data-hint="The published schedule presents the arrival as expected, so use when." data-fix="When the coordinator arrives, she’ll open the office."><p class="quiz-question">4. The published schedule treats the coordinator’s arrival as expected. Which sentence matches that framing?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="When the coordinator arrives, she’ll open the office.">When the coordinator arrives, she’ll open the office.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="If the coordinator might arrive, she’ll open the office.">If the coordinator might arrive, she’ll open the office.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="When the coordinator will arrive, she’ll open the office.">When the coordinator will arrive, she’ll open the office.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect and retrieve</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the decision path without looking back</h3>
    <p>What does the condition activate? Why is the condition open rather than automatically unlikely? Which result forms can follow it? How do <span class="ex">if</span>, expected-time <span class="ex">when</span>, and exception marker <span class="ex">unless</span> frame the future differently?</p>
  </div>
  <p class="note-line">Return tomorrow before rereading. Complete the <a href="#next-day-retrieval">five-minute next-day retrieval</a>, then revisit only the condition form, result purpose, marker, clause order, punctuation, or spoken boundary that still feels slow.</p>

